blican baseline.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Bill Cassidy (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Louisiana's open Senate seat favors Republican Julia Letlow, a congresswoman who has raised over $6 million and drawn heavy outside spending from groups on both sides. Democrat Jamie Davis has raised about $2 million but faces a state that backed Republicans by double digits in recent cycles. Bill Cassidy's loss of renomination added some uncertainty, and one Democratic-sponsored poll in September showed Letlow ahead by only four points, drawing attention.\n\nStill, ten expert ratings place the race in the Safe or Solid Republican column, and prediction markets give Davis less than a one-in-ten chance. The race is Letlow's to lose, with the main question being the size of her winning margin rather than the outcome itself.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0491, "margin": -9.91}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0664, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0312, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0328, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0575, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0895, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0752, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0962, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.1593, "margin": -6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0833, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0984, "margin": -8.0}]}